= Source =

All PHP, JavaScript and CSS sources ship unminified in this plugin. JavaScript uses WordPress-provided editor dependencies. No compilation or bundled React is required. The external /embed.js source and protocol are maintained by the service, independently of this plugin.

== Installation ==

1. In WordPress, open Plugins > Add New, search for @@NAME@@, click Install Now and activate the plugin. You can also upload the plugin ZIP manually.
2. Click Get started in the plugin list, or open Settings > @@NAME@@, and read the three setup steps and service/privacy disclosure.
3. Save a form in your organizer account, copy its public URL, add the block or shortcode and publish.
4. Preview the published page, including mobile layout and the standalone link.

== Frequently Asked Questions ==

= Is the plugin free? =
Yes. The WordPress plugin is free. The @@NAME@@ service has separate organizer pricing and terms, available at @@OFFER_URL@@. An organizer account is required.

= Do I need WooCommerce? =
No. The plugin embeds the public @@NAME@@ form directly using its Gutenberg block or shortcode. No WooCommerce installation or service API keys are required.

= Can I sell tickets with assigned seats? =
Yes, when your event form includes a seating plan configured in @@NAME@@. The embedded form displays the service's seat selection and availability.

= Can I manage orders in WordPress? =
No. Sign in to @@NAME@@ to manage events and orders.

= Does a visitor need a WordPress account? =
No. The public form runs in the service iframe. Event-specific requirements are controlled by the service.

= Why was my URL rejected? =
Use the exact saved public form URL on @@ORIGIN@@. Other domains, personal links, fragments, query parameters and administration URLs are rejected. Development origins require explicit local WordPress configuration and cannot be supplied in block attributes.

= What if my site's security policy blocks embedding? =
Allow @@ORIGIN@@ in frame-src and, for the helper, script-src. Do not add an unverified iframe sandbox. Use fixed mode or the standalone link if necessary. Never automatically repeat a purchase after an uncertain result; check with the organizer first.

= What happens on deactivation or deletion? =
The plugin owns no tables, options or remote orders, and performs no remote writes on activation, deactivation or uninstall. Service orders remain. Deactivation can expose raw shortcode text; remove the block/shortcode or replace it with a normal public link.

